.TH "bathconvert" 1 "@BATH_DATE@" "BATH @BATH_VERSION@" "BATH Manual"

.SH NAME
bathconvert \- convert profile file to various formats


.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bathconvert
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I hmmfile_out
.I hmmfile_in


.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
The
.B bathconvert
utility converts an input profile file to different formats.

.PP
By default, the input profile can be in any HMMER/BATH format,
including older ASCII or binary formats. The output is written in
current HMMER3 ASCII format, which is the format used by
.B bathsearch
and other BATH tools.

.PP
.I hmmfile_in
may be '\-' (dash), which means reading this input from stdin rather
than a file.


.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-h
Help; print a brief reminder of command line usage and all available
options.

.TP
.BI \-\-ct " <n>"
Use the alternate genetic code specified by NCBI translation table
number
.IR <n>
when processing the profile. The default is 1 (the standard genetic
code).

.TP
.B \-\-fs
Calculate the frameshift-aware E-value statistics (FS3/FS5) needed to
use the resulting profile with
.BR "bathsearch \-\-fs" ,
if they are not already present. They are also recalculated whenever
.B \-\-ct
changes the codon table, whether or not
.B \-\-fs
is given, since existing statistics would otherwise be for the wrong
table. If the profile already has valid statistics and
.B \-\-ct
does not change the table,
.B \-\-fs
has no effect.

.TP
.B \-\-addstats
Calculate the standard E-value statistics (MSV, Viterbi and Forward)
for a profile built with
.BR "bathbuild \-\-nostats" ,
so it can be used with
.BR bathsearch .
Has no effect if the profile already has them.
.B \-\-fs
also adds them to such a profile, along with the frameshift statistics.


.SH SEE ALSO

.BR bathsearch (1),
.BR bathbuild (1),
.BR bathfetch (1),
.BR bathstat (1),
.BR bathemit (1),
.BR bathalign (1)

.PP
For complete documentation, see the BATH repository:
https://github.com/TravisWheelerLab/BATH


